  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="452e871a-eca4-5956-b1b5-b986d603c095" activityNameId="82d8fca9-245f-5b69-b566-153b499ec475" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Kenaf fibres, at farm</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Kenaf fibres, at farm
Production of Kenaf delivers the co-products 'kenaf fibres, at farm' and 'kenaf stalks, from fibre production, at farm'. An allocation was carried out based on economical and mass criteria ;
UUID: 93114821-4443-3770-ad34-b3bb8b11ed93
The inventories include the mainly manual cultivation of Kenaf from conventional production standards. Included steps are soil cultivation, pesticides fertilisation (mineral fertilizer), harvest, loading for transport and extraction of the fibres after retting process. 
Location: Data from expert panel Indian Jute Institute and experts assumptions. India is the most important producers of Kenaf fibres
Technology: Cultivation of kenaf from conventional production standards
Time period: undefined
Production volume: World production 2000: 0.51 Mio. t  (China: 0.244 Mio t  / India: 0.2 Mio t)
Sampling: Expert interviews, literature data and assumptions. 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_93114821-4443-3770-ad34-b3bb8b11ed93.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
